    "created_at": "2022-11-02T02:17:24Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-11-02T02:17:24Z",
    "body": "In #8460 I decided to export \"child navigable\", but not \"nested navigable\". I think that might be more correct for other specs, which want to talk about the general concept of child navigables, not about the specific \"nested navigable\" field that navigable containers have?\r\n\r\nIf fenced frames actually wants to use nested navigable, that's probably a symptom of it being a monkey-patch spec, which will in general depend on lots of non-exported terms. So I would lean toward closing this until we have a clearer example of someone that actually needs to reach into a navigable container's nested navigable...",
